# TypeScript Standards

## Type Definitions
```typescript
// Export interfaces from types/index.ts
export interface Company {
  id: string
  _id?: string  // MongoDB ID
  name: string
  status: CompanyStatus
}

// Use type for unions/aliases
export type CompanyStatus = 'pending' | 'active' | 'inactive' | 'archived'

// Form data types (separate from entity types)
export interface CreateCompanyFormData {
  name: string
  email: string
}

export interface UpdateCompanyFormData {
  name?: string  // Optional for partial updates
  email?: string
}
```

## Naming Conventions
- Interfaces: `PascalCase` (e.g., `Company`, `UserProfile`)
- Types: `PascalCase` (e.g., `CompanyStatus`)
- Functions: `camelCase` (e.g., `fetchCompanies`)
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` (e.g., `COUNTRIES`)
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `company-management.tsx`)

## NEVER Use `any`
```typescript
// NEVER
const data: any = response
function handle(input: any) {}

// ALWAYS type properly or use `unknown` and narrow
const data: Company = response.data
function handle(input: unknown) {
  if (isCompany(input)) { /* now typed */ }
}
```

## Error Handling

### Frontend -- always show user feedback
```typescript
try {
  const result = await api.create(data)
  if (!result.success) throw new Error(result.error)
  toast({ title: t('success.created') })
} catch (error) {
  toast({ title: t('error.createFailed'), variant: 'destructive' })
}
```

### Backend -- throw typed errors (caught by error handler)
```typescript
// Throw specific error classes (from utils/errors.ts)
if (!auth.companyId) {
  throw new ForbiddenError('No company associated');
}

const item = await Model.findById(id);
if (!item) throw new NotFoundError('Lead');

// Zod validation errors are caught automatically
const data = schema.parse(body); // throws ZodError -> 400
```

### NEVER swallow errors silently
```typescript
// NEVER
try { await api.call() } catch (e) {}

// ALWAYS handle or rethrow
try {
  await api.call()
} catch (e) {
  toast({ title: t('error.failed'), variant: 'destructive' })
}
```

## Avoid
- `any` type -- use `unknown` and narrow
- Non-null assertions `!` -- use optional chaining `?.`
- Implicit returns in complex functions
- `as` type assertions unless absolutely necessary (prefer type guards)
